    "final_message": "`scripts/verify story-drafting` passes, and both acceptance tests pass unchanged. Tessercheck reports zero findings, `mypy --strict` is clean, 73 non-root tests pass, and the 2 root tests pass against the host served on :9350. The work is committed as `a264811` on the current branch, and only my four files changed.\n\n**Domain** (`story-drafting/drafting/domain/jtbd.py`):\n- **New value objects:**\n  - `StoryText` is built from a `StoryTextSpec`. Its only behaviour is producing a drafted `StoryView`.\n  - `StoryTexts` is a collection built whole from the `RecordStoriesSpec`. It reports its length and turns every text into a drafted `StoryView`.\n- **`record_stories`:**\n  - If the job to be done already holds stories, it answers `ALREADY_RECORDED`, so stories are recorded only once.\n  - If no story texts are given, it answers `NONE_GIVEN` and records nothing.\n  - Otherwise it keeps each text as a story in state `drafted` and answers `RECORDED`.\n- **`status`** follows from the stories' states:\n  - no stories \u2192 `drafting_stories`\n  - any story drafted \u2192 `awaiting_story_acceptance`\n  - stories, none drafted \u2192 `stories_decided`\n- **Tests** (`test_jtbd.py`): a completeness test, the three statuses, and recording for each outcome (drafted stories kept, none given, recorded twice).\n\n**Drafter** (`story-drafting/drafting/adapters/gateways/template_story_drafter.py`): it writes one story text from the job to be done:\n- given: `I am {role}`\n- when: `I want {i_want}`\n- then: `so that {so_that}`\n\nIts test checks that at least one story text comes back, and the exact text.\n\n**GAP:** none. The contract had everything these two stories need.\n\nOne thing I noticed: the generated `JtbdActions.record_stories` always builds a fresh `Jtbd` with no stories instead of loading the saved one. So `ALREADY_RECORDED` can't happen through the app today, and a retried record would overwrite the stories. The two stories don't depend on this, but \"done once\" in the language isn't enforced end to end. Fix"
  },
